+// SSL_set_reality_server_ignore_sigalgs configures |ssl|, a server, to select
+// its CertificateVerify signature algorithm from the local certificate's key
+// alone, mirroring the xtls/reality fork: the fork's TLS 1.3 server signs the
+// one-time REALITY certificate's CertificateVerify with Ed25519 without
+// consulting the client's signature_algorithms, and utls/xray REALITY clients
+// accept (and verify) that signature without having advertised ed25519. Stock
+// boring would instead abort with NO_COMMON_SIGNATURE_ALGORITHMS. Only
+// affects which algorithm the server signs with; the signature itself is
+// verified against the certificate's public key as usual. Call it before
+// starting the handshake.
+OPENSSL_EXPORT void SSL_set_reality_server_ignore_sigalgs(SSL *ssl);
+
